menu "OrcSDR receivers"

    config ORCSDR_MAX_RECEIVERS
        int "RTL-SDR receivers this build runs (1 to 4)"
        range 1 4
        default 1
        help
            One radio task per receiver; each receiver takes the next dongle attached. With 1 the firmware behaves as it
            always did (six 16 KiB USB transfers). With more than one, each receiver uses two 16 KiB internal USB DMA
            transfers (the setting the four-dongle validation used) and USB clients are split across both cores.
            The code supports up to 4, but how many this console can run at once alongside the UI, Wi-Fi and audio is
            not yet measured. Check "RTL_MEM STATUS" dma_free, "RTL_CPU" and the per-receiver drops from
            "RTL_RX STATUS" with the console running before choosing more than 1 or 2.

    config ORCSDR_ETHERNET
        bool "Wired Ethernet (RMII PHY) from the board profile"
        default n
        help
            Compiles the Ethernet driver. It starts only if the selected board profile lists Ethernet pins (the Waveshare
            ESP32-P4-ETH, -POE-ETH and Module-DEV-KIT profiles do). The pins are the documented ones; they are not verified on a
            board until a link comes up, and the PHY chip is tried as IP101 first, then the generic driver. Off by default so a
            board behaves exactly as before unless this is chosen.

endmenu
